# Data Schema — Spenvo

Document version: **1.4** (M1 + Usuario/nombreUsuario, slices 1-9/10 + ARCH-M501 Room v4). Status: baseline draft, versioned with every change.

## 1. Source of truth and model

Two stores, one domain model:

- **Firestore** — remote source of truth (collections below). Writes via native
  offline cache. Deny-by-default rules with server-side roles (draft in
  `firestore.rules`, final in M3).
- **Room + SQLCipher** — encrypted local presentation cache. Provided by `:core:data`.
  Room JSON exports are versioned in `core/data/schemas/<package>.<DB>/`.

Golden rule: **the UI always reads from Room; writes go to Firestore**.
Conflict: LWW with `editedBy`/`editedAt` (server-set) + visible conflict in the UI.

## 2. Firestore (draft v1.0)

### ER (Mermaid)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USUARIOS ||--o{ ACCESO_PLAN : "accesses"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ ACCESO_PLAN : "is accessed by"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ CATEGORIAS : "has"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ GASTOS : "has"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ INGRESOS : "has"
    CATEGORIAS ||--o{ GASTOS : "classifies"
    CATEGORIAS ||--o{ INGRESOS : "classifies"
```

### Collections

#### `usuarios/{usuarioId}` (`uid`/`nombreUsuario` added, `nombre`/`email` made nullable in
Usuario/nombreUsuario slice 1/10; rules revised in slice 9/10)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| uid | string | same value as the doc ID; rules check `request.resource.data.uid == usuarioId` |
| nombreUsuario | string | unique public handle, display-cased (e.g. `GatoAzul42`) |
| nombre | string? | null for an anonymous session |
| email | string? | null for an anonymous session; never null once registered (enforced by construction — the only write path that sets it is `vincularEmail`, which requires it) |
| avatarUrl | string? | M7 (Storage) |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |

Rules: `get` open to any authenticated user (plan co-members need to resolve each other's
`nombreUsuario`); `list` always denied — an open `list` would let anyone dump every user's
`email`/`nombre` via `orderBy`/`limit`, defeating `emails_usuario`'s whole purpose below.
`create`/`update` owner-only.

#### `nombres_usuario/{nombreUsuarioNormalizado}` and `emails_usuario/{emailNormalizado}`
(added Usuario/nombreUsuario slice 3/10, rules in slice 9/10)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| usuarioId | string | the uid that reserved this normalized nombreUsuario/email |

Lookup indexes, not user-facing data — the doc ID *is* the normalized (lowercase/trimmed) key,
and its existence *is* the uniqueness guarantee. `nombres_usuario` entries are created/deleted via
a client transaction (`intentarReservarNombreUsuario`/`renombrar`); `emails_usuario` entries are
written once alongside `vincularEmail` (no reservation transaction needed — Firebase Auth already
guarantees email uniqueness at the identity level). Rules: `get` open to any authenticated user,
`list` always denied (same enumeration risk as `usuarios` above), `create`/`delete` owner-only,
`update` always denied (an overwrite attempt on an existing doc is classified by Firestore as
`update`, not `create`, so this is what actually blocks reservation hijacking, not just client
transaction discipline).

#### `invitaciones_pendientes_por_email/{emailNormalizado}_{planId}` (added Usuario/nombreUsuario
slice 7/10, rules in slice 9/10)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| email | string | normalized (lowercase/trimmed) |
| planId | string | |
| rol | enum | `owner` \| `admin` \| `editor` \| `viewer` |
| invitadoPor | string | inviter's uid |
| createdAt | timestamp | |

Written when `InvitarMiembroUseCase` resolves an email that has no matching `usuarioId` yet;
consumed (converted to a real `acceso_plan_financiero` doc via the self-grant rule below, then
deleted) by `AsegurarUsuarioUseCase.paraVincularEmail` once that email registers. No
`nombres_usuario`-miss equivalent — see the design doc's "Invite by nombreUsuario or email"
section for why. Rules: `get` always denied (never looked up by ID directly); `list` restricted to
a query whose `email` equality filter matches the caller's own verified `request.auth.token.email`
— Firestore denies any `list`/`getDocs` call that doesn't include that matching filter, so this
can't be used to enumerate other people's pending invites; `create` open to any authenticated
user (anyone can invite); `delete` restricted to the matching-email caller (cleanup after
resolving); no `update`.

#### `planes_financieros/{planId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| nombre | string | |
| descripcion | string? | |
| moneda | string | ISO 4217 code |
| createdBy | string | creator uid |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |
| editedBy | string | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | timestamp | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | soft-delete |

#### `acceso_plan_financiero/{usuarioId}_{planId}` (N:M pivot)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| usuarioId | string | uid |
| planId | string | |
| rol | enum | `owner` \| `admin` \| `editor` \| `viewer` |
| invitacionEstado | enum | `pendiente` \| `aceptada` (M3) |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |

`create` rules (as of Usuario/nombreUsuario slice 9/10): the plan's `owner` on plan creation, an
existing `admin`+ inviting a member, or — new in slice 9/10 — the caller self-granting exactly the
`rol` named in a matching `invitaciones_pendientes_por_email` doc for their own verified email
(how a pending-by-email invite from slice 7/10 actually gets consumed; without this third case
that resolution path always failed with `PERMISSION_DENIED` once rules were enforced).

#### `categorias/{categoriaId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| planId | string | scoped to the plan |
| nombre | string | |
| icono | string | default icon key (M4) |
| iconoUrl | string? | custom icon (M7) |
| tipo | enum | `gasto` \| `ingreso` |
| editedBy | string | |
| editedAt | timestamp | |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | |

#### `gastos/{gastoId}` and `ingresos/{ingresoId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| planId | string | |
| categoriaId | string | |
| monto | number | in minor units of the currency (cents) |
| fecha | date | movement date |
| descripcion | string? | |
| creadoPor | string | uid |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |
| editedBy | string | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | timestamp | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | soft-delete |

### Cross-cutting conventions
- Amounts always in **minor units** (cents) to avoid floating-point errors.
- `deletedAt != null` = soft-deleted; rules filter it and the UI does not show it.
- `editedBy`/`editedAt` are written by Firestore (rules) with `request.auth.uid` and `request.time`;
  the client never chooses them.

## 3. Room (version 4)

Room is the encrypted local cache. Schema exports are versioned in
`core/data/schemas/com.agoitdev.spenvo.data.local.SpenvoDatabase/` (`1.json`, `2.json`, `3.json`, `4.json`).

### `sync_state` (v1, unchanged)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | singleton `"default"` |
| lastSyncedAtMillis | INTEGER? | sync metadata (M1/M2) |

### `usuarios` (new in v2, `nombreUsuario` + nullable `nombre`/`email` in v3)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | uid |
| nombreUsuario | TEXT | unique public handle, generated on first sign-in (v3) |
| nombre | TEXT? | null for an anonymous session (v3: was non-null in v2) |
| email | TEXT? | null for an anonymous session (v3: was non-null in v2) |
| avatarUrl | TEXT? | M7 (Storage) |
| createdAt | INTEGER | epoch millis |
| updatedAt | INTEGER | |

### `planes_financieros` (new in v2)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | |
| nombre | TEXT | |
| descripcion | TEXT? | |
| moneda | TEXT | ISO 4217 code |
| createdBy | TEXT | creator uid |
| createdAt | INTEGER | |
| updatedAt | INTEGER | |
| editedBy | TEXT? | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | INTEGER? | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | INTEGER? | soft-delete |

### `acceso_plan_financiero` (new in v2, N:M pivot)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| usuarioId | TEXT (PK, part 1) | uid |
| planId | TEXT (PK, part 2) | |
| rol | TEXT | `owner` \| `admin` \| `editor` \| `viewer` |
| invitacionEstado | TEXT | `pendiente` \| `aceptada` (M3) |
| createdAt | INTEGER | |
| updatedAt | INTEGER | |

### `categorias` (new in v2)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | |
| planId | TEXT | scoped to the plan |
| nombre | TEXT | |
| icono | TEXT | default icon key (M4) |
| iconoUrl | TEXT? | custom icon (M7) |
| tipo | TEXT | `gasto` \| `ingreso` |
| editedBy | TEXT? | |
| editedAt | INTEGER? | |
| deletedAt | INTEGER? | |
| Index | `planId, tipo` | `index_categorias_planId_tipo` |

### `gastos` and `ingresos` (new in v2)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | |
| planId | TEXT | |
| categoriaId | TEXT | |
| montoUnidadesMenores | INTEGER | in minor units of the currency |
| fecha | TEXT | movement date (ISO) |
| descripcion | TEXT? | |
| creadoPor | TEXT | uid |
| createdAt | INTEGER | |
| updatedAt | INTEGER | |
| editedBy | TEXT? | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | INTEGER? | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | INTEGER? | soft-delete |
| Index | `planId, fecha` | `index_gastos_planId_fecha` / `index_ingresos_planId_fecha` |

### `ediciones_pendientes` (new in v4, ARCH-M501)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| clave | TEXT (PK) | `"$coleccion:$id"`, e.g. `gastos:g1` |
| tipo | TEXT | `GASTO` \| `INGRESO` \| `CATEGORIA` \| `PLAN` |
| editorId | TEXT | uid of the local edit's author |
| base | INTEGER? | `editedAt` of the row read before the local write, epoch millis |
| miEditedAt | INTEGER? | `editedAt` the local write is expected to echo back, epoch millis |

Room-backed replacement for the process-lifetime-only `EdicionesPendientes` in-memory registry —
closes the process-death data-loss gap (see `doc/architecture.md`). No `miVersion` column: the
local snapshot is reconstructed from the corresponding main-table row at conflict-detection time
instead, since the write-path transaction guarantees both are always in sync.

### `conflictos_pendientes` (new in v4, ARCH-M501)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| clave | TEXT (PK) | `"$coleccion:$id"` |
| registroId | TEXT | the entity's own id |
| tipo | TEXT | `GASTO` \| `INGRESO` \| `CATEGORIA` \| `PLAN` |
| local | TEXT | `SnapshotConflicto` as JSON (kotlinx-serialization, epoch-millis DTO) |
| remoto | TEXT | `SnapshotConflicto` as JSON, same converter |

Room-backed replacement for the process-lifetime-only `ConflictosPendientes` in-memory registry —
same rationale as `ediciones_pendientes` above. `local`/`remoto` are stored via a new
`Converters.snapshotConflictoToJson`/`jsonToSnapshotConflicto` `@TypeConverter` pair, since
`SnapshotConflicto.editadoEn: Instant?` has no built-in kotlinx-serialization support.

### Migration v1 → v2
`SpenvoDatabase.MIGRATION_1_2` creates the six new tables and three indexes above;
`sync_state` is preserved. Validated by an instrumented migration test
(`SpenvoDatabaseMigrationTest`, SQLCipher + `MigrationTestHelper`) and by the Room
exported schema (`2.json`).

### Migration v2 → v3
`SpenvoDatabase.MIGRATION_2_3` reshapes `usuarios` only: adds `nombreUsuario TEXT NOT NULL
DEFAULT ''` (the public handle) and relaxes `nombre`/`email` to nullable, since an anonymous
session has neither. SQLite cannot alter a column's nullability in place, so each of those two
columns is renamed to `*_old`, re-added as nullable `TEXT`, copied over with an `UPDATE`, and
the `*_old` column dropped. Every other table is untouched. Validated by the same instrumented
migration test (`SpenvoDatabaseMigrationTest`) and by the Room exported schema (`3.json`).

### Migration v3 → v4
`SpenvoDatabase.MIGRATION_3_4` creates the two new tables above (`ediciones_pendientes`,
`conflictos_pendientes`) via raw `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, matching `MIGRATION_1_2`'s style —
no destructive migration, every existing table untouched. Validated by the same instrumented
migration test (`SpenvoDatabaseMigrationTest`) and by the Room exported schema (`4.json`).

### Version plan
- **v1 (M0)**: `sync_state` — validates the Room+KSP+SQLCipher toolchain.
- **v2 (M1)**: local domain entities (users, plans, categories, expenses,
  income) as cache; indexes; `editedBy/editedAt`.
- **v3 (Usuario/nombreUsuario)**: `usuarios` becomes a live synced entity — `nombreUsuario`
  added, `nombre`/`email` made nullable.
- **v4 (ARCH-M501)**: `ediciones_pendientes`/`conflictos_pendientes` added — Room becomes the
  durable single source of truth for pending-edit/conflict registries, closing the process-death
  data-loss gap the prior in-memory-only registries carried.
- Migrations with `Migration` + SQLCipher (upgrade test included).

## 4. Firestore indexes (draft)

See `firestore.indexes.json`. Rules:
- Index by `planId + fecha` on `gastos` and `ingresos` (monthly listings).
- Index by `planId + tipo` on `categorias`.
- No wildcard indexes.

## 5. Change control

| Date | Doc version | Schema | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2026-08-19 | 1.0 | Room v1 / Firestore draft | M0 baseline |
| 2026-08-20 | 1.1 | Room v2 | M1 — local entities as cache (migration v1→v2, validated) |
| 2026-08-30 | 1.2 | Firestore | Usuario/nombreUsuario slice 7/10 — added `invitaciones_pendientes_por_email` collection (anti-enumeration invite-by-email pending state) |
| 2026-08-30 | 1.3 | Room v3 / Firestore | Usuario/nombreUsuario slices 1-9/10 — Room migration v2→v3 on `usuarios` (`nombreUsuario` added, `nombre`/`email` nullable); Firestore `usuarios` splits `get` (open to any authenticated caller) from `list` (denied) and gains the `nombres_usuario`/`emails_usuario` uniqueness-and-lookup index collections plus `invitaciones_pendientes_por_email`; `acceso_plan_financiero.create` gains the pending-invite self-grant disjunct so a newly-registered invitee can materialize their own access |
| 2026-08-30 | 1.3 | Firestore rules | Pre-merge security fixes (no schema change): `invitaciones_pendientes_por_email.create` now requires admin(2)+ on the plan, `invitadoPor == uid` and a doc id matching its own `email_planId` (closes a privilege-escalation chain through the self-grant disjunct); `list`/`delete` compare against `request.auth.token.email.lower()`; `usuarios.create`/`update` require an owned `nombres_usuario` reservation for the written handle (closes `nombreUsuario` impersonation) |
| 2026-09-02 | 1.4 | Room v4 | ARCH-M501 (Task 3) — Room migration v3→v4 adds `ediciones_pendientes`/`conflictos_pendientes`, the durable backing store for the pending-edit/conflict registries (closes the process-death data-loss gap in `doc/architecture.md`); new `EdicionPendienteEntity`/`ConflictoEdicionEntity`, `EdicionPendienteDao`/`ConflictoEdicionDao`, and a `SnapshotConflicto` JSON `@TypeConverter` pair in `Converters.kt` |